{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794589425766,"sessionID":"ses_e2a22a260ffeYYaYAltxo2QfKV","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5dd80490020O3ozYL4sdyktH","sessionID":"ses_e2a22a260ffeYYaYAltxo2QfKV","messageID":"msg_1d5dd677c001IfYx0yhRgHq7kb","type":"tool","id":"call_00_ET_fKmQ1I2IiwT5AbqEBFyT0354","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md, lines 1-141\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 17: review-pass-two-remediation\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that fix the 27 P2 findings of review pass two in nine parallel worker lanes and one coordinator edit: the shared no-edit gate, the behaviour runner's backfill and restore, measurement hygiene, the scorer, playbook and plugin text, the subprocess busy scan, the doctor contracts and the doctor checks, each with a failing-then-passing test where one can exist.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"review pass two remediation tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 17: review-pass-two-remediation\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a gate, a rebuild, a full-suite run, a parent spec edit or the close-out. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says `in ADV`. A short name stands for the path or command below. Set the path names once with `export ADV=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime RAD=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy SKA=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor DS=.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts DA=.skilled/commands/doctor/assets SP=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch PL=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/planning`.\n30: - `G` is `git -c core.fsmonitor=false`. `BASE` is the commit T001 records with `G rev-parse --short HEAD`, so a diff against it covers committed and uncommitted lane work. `TSX` is `--import ./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/node_modules/tsx/dist/loader.mjs`, so `node TSX <file>` runs a TypeScript probe.\n31: - `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `VX <file>` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <file>` in `ADV`, with `<file>` relative to `ADV`. `VALL` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed.\n32: - `NT <file>` is `node --test <file>`. `DALL` is `node --test $DS/tests/*.test.cjs`, `VSR` is `node --test .skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/*.test.mjs` and `VP` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs`, and each must report `fail 0`.\n33: - `DERIVE` is `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -c '{status, changed}'`, which must print `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}`. `RV` is `bash $DS/route-validate.sh` and `SRM` is `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, which must exit 0. `PBV` is `node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-manual-testing-playbook/scripts/validate-playbook-package.cjs --package $SKA/manual-testing-playbook`, which must print a line starting `PASS package=system-skill-advisor`.\n34: - `FLOOR` is `node $RAD/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.typed, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune'`, which printed `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}` and `{\"own\":8,\"attached\":15,\"combined\":23,\"total\":45}` at planning. `EVAL` is `node $RAD/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which printed `[160,50,21,5]`. Phase 016 may change either, so T001 records the real before lines.\n35: - `A10Q` is `node $DS/agents-md-check.cjs --root . --json | jq -r '.rows[] | select(.id==\"A10\") | \"\\(.detail) | pass \\([.entries[] | select(.state==\"PASS\")] | length) | reported \\([.entries[] | select(.state==\"INFO\" and .kind!=\"pointer missing\")] | length)\"'`, which printed `5/6 copies as expected, 1 pointer missing | pass 3 | reported 2` at planning.\n36: - WG1: `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `TX` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/text.ts` and `FU` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`. `CAG` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `ROE` is `$ADV/tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts`, `CMA` is `$ADV/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`, `CAT` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` and `AST` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`. `DER` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `CBR` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` and `DCS` is `$ADV/tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` (new). `SINGLE(m)` is the helper `CAG` already defines, `{ action: 'route', selectionKind: 'single', targets: [{ workflowMode: m }] }`. `NOEDIT4` is the four endings `don't change anything yet`, `no changes yet`, `don\\u2019t touch any files` and `make no changes`, where `\\u2019` is written as that escape inside a test string, so the test holds a curly apostrophe and the source stays ASCII.\n37: - WG2: `CO` is `$RAD/command-offer.mjs`, `COT` is `$ADV/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`, `WR` is `$RAD/worktree-restore.mjs`, `WRT` is `$ADV/tests/worktree-restore.vitest.ts`, `R` is `$RAD/run-command-behaviour.mjs` and `BG` is `$ADV/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts`. `MARK` is the file name `skilled-behaviour-arena`.\n38: - WG3: `CAP` is `$RAD/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `SLT` is `$ADV/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`, `MBC` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` and `MBCT` is `$ADV/tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts`. `ENV9` is the nine names `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR`, `SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLE_BUILTIN_SEMANTIC`, `VITEST`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE`, `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON`, `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON`, `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_BM25_LEXICAL_SHADOW` and `SPECKIT_PRIVATE_SKILL_ROOTS`.\n39: - WG4: `S` is `$RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `CTS` is `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `RA` is `$RAD/README.md`.\n40: - WG5: `PB` is `$SKA/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`, `PBT` is `$ADV/tests/manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` and `TR` is `$ADV/tests/README.md`.\n41: - WG6: `PJ` is `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `PJT` is `.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs` and `ENV` is `$ADV/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts`.\n42: - WG7: `SUB` is `$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts`, `SUBT` is `$ADV/tests/subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` and `ARM` is `$SKA/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`.\n43: - WG8: `DAE` is `$DA/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml`, `RTS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`, `DSM` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md`, `DAC` is `$DS/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs` and `DSCT` is `$DS/tests/doctor-setup-contract.test.cjs`.\n44: - WG9: `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, `HWT` is `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`, `CHK` is `$DS/agents-md-check.cjs` and `CHKT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs`.\n45: - WG10: `PS` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md`.\n46: - `SP` holds this phase's records and `PL` holds the 18 planning probes. Each probe's first comment line says how to run it, and each builds and removes its own temporary trees.\n47: \n48: Rules for every task:\n49: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test writes the test case first, runs it and sees it fail for the reason the task names, then makes the change and sees it pass. Its verify names both runs. A task that says its case passes today adds a guard and changes no code.\n50: - Re-read every file a task names before the first edit. Phase 016 edited some of them after this plan was written. When a line, string or name the task quotes is not in the file, change nothing and mark the task `[B]` with the line found in its place.\n51: - No test input or expected output names `/create:skill` or `/create:sk-skill`. Use `/create:agent` or `/create:readme`.\n52: - No task reads or prints the prompt text of a row whose `split` is `holdout`, and no task opens `holdout-prompts.jsonl`.\n53: - No worker runs a build, the full suite, a daemon or a model session (`claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `devin`, `dsh`), runs a live arm, approves a Codex hook or writes under the home folder. A test builds its trees under the system temp folder and removes them.\n54: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a finding id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T040 checks it.\n55: - Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, `PS`, another phase folder, any `package.json`, any routing corpus, any committed baseline or a file another lane owns. Add no dependency.\n56: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write. A doc sentence holds no em dash and no semicolon.\n57: - Run Vitest with `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD` unless a task says otherwise, because a dispatched worker inherits `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`.\n58: - When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n59: \n60: Worker lanes. A lane is one worker running its tasks in the order listed. The lanes own different files and run in parallel. Each task owns the files in its parentheses.\n61: - Setup, the coordinator: T001, T002.\n62: - Wave 1, nine worker lanes and the coordinator, all in parallel after T002. WG1: T003, T004, T005, T006, T007, T008, T009. WG2: T010, T011, T012, T013. WG3: T014, T015. WG4: T016, T017, T018, T019, T020, T021. WG5: T022, T023, T024. WG6: T025, T026, T027, T028. WG7: T029, T030. WG8: T031, T032, T033. WG9: T034, T035. Coordinator: T036.\n63: - Verification, one at a time after every wave 1 lane ends: T037, T038, T039, T040, T041, all `[C]`.\n64: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n69: ## Phase 1: Setup\n70: \n71: - [x] T001 [C] Confirm phase 016 is committed and record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `G log -1 --format=%h -- .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `test -e .skilled/commands/create/skill.md`, `G status --porcelain -- .skilled .opencode AGENTS.md` and `G rev-parse --short HEAD`, then `npm run build` in `ADV`, `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `A10Q`, `TC`, `VALL`, `DALL`, `VSR`, `VP`, `DERIVE`, `RV`, `SRM` and `PBV`, and write each command with its last output lines or its exit code into `before.txt`. When phase 016 is not committed or a gate is red, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held. Verify: the `log` prints a hash, `test -e` exits 1, the `status` prints nothing, the build, `TC`, `RV` and `SRM` exit 0, `FLOOR` prints typed recall `correct` at least 24 of 44, false offers `count` 0 of 35, typed `combined` 44 of 44 and plain tune `combined` at least 23 of 45, `EVAL` prints no value below `[160,50,21]` in its first three places and a fourth no higher than 5, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `DALL`, `VSR` and `VP` report `fail 0`, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}`, `PBV` prints its `PASS` line and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 17.\n72: - [x] T002 [C] Record the reproductions (`$SP/repro-before.txt`). Run each of the 18 probes in `PL` as its first comment line says, with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset, and append each command, its output and its exit code. Verify: `rg -cF -e 'attach \"make no changes\" -> \"/create:agent\"' -e 'scorer commandMeaningEligible \"make no changes\" -> true' -e 'fake CLI ran: true, fake hook ran: true' -e 'left on disk: notes draft.md true, plain.md false' -e '--row-id g2-deep-review-ask -> arm pre' -e 'run line records the fixture: false' -e 'hook saw AI_SESSION_CHILD=1' -e 'marker after 1 MiB: errorCode NON_ZERO_EXIT, retriesAttempted 0' -e 'bash -lc: exit 1 hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json' -e 'workflow names the restore failure: 0' -e 'route names the temporary-directory fallback: no' -e 'privacy case persists a record: false' -e 'LF: raw break in literal true, parses false' -e 'variables left changed: [\"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE\"' -e 'plugin test asserts a command label: false' -e 'note: the source category tree contains 41' -e 'handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563 =>' $SP/repro-before.txt` prints 17 and every recorded exit code is 0.\n73: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n78: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n79: \n80: ### Wave 1, lane WG1: the shared no-edit gate and bridge text\n81: - [ ] T003 [P] Widen the shared no-edit pattern and add `isNoEditRequest` (`CA`, `CAG`). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('command attach on a no-edit prompt')`, add `it.each(NOEDIT4)('offers no hub command when the prompt ends %s', ...)` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-agent'), 'use sk-doc to create an agent called invoice-parser, ' + ending)` to be `undefined`, add `it('offers the agent command when the prompt asks for the change')` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-agent'), 'use sk-doc to create an agent called invoice-parser')` to be `'/create:agent'`, and add `it('reads a curly apostrophe as a straight one')` expecting `isNoEditRequest('Don\\u2019t touch any files')` to be `true` and `isNoEditRequest('touch the files')` to be `false`, importing `isNoEditRequest` beside `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the four `it.each` cases return `'/create:agent'` and the helper case fail. Then in `CA` replace the `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` literal with `/\\b(no edits?|no changes|without making changes|(?:do not|don't) (change|edit|modify|touch)|read-only only|no edits yet|only; do not|just show|just list)\\b/`, add below it `export function isNoEditRequest(text: string): boolean` returning `NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(text.toLowerCase().replace(/[\\u2018\\u2019]/g, \"'\"))` with a comment that many keyboards type the contraction with a curly apostrophe, and replace `if (NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(prompt.toLowerCase())) return undefined;` in `attachCommand` with `if (isNoEditRequest(prompt)) return undefined;`. Verify: the first `VX` run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `rg -c \"^import\" $CA` prints nothing.\n82: - [ ] T004 [P] Route the explainer test through the shared helper (`TX`, `ROE`). Test first: in `ROE`, add `it.each([...])('treats a read-only request that rules out a change as read-only: %s', ...)` over `please show me the parser config, don't change anything yet`, `please show me the parser config so i can update it later, no changes yet`, `please show me what the fix would be, don\\u2019t touch any files` and `please show me the parser config and what to edit, make no changes`, each expecting `isReadOnlyExplainer(prompt.toLowerCase())` to be `true`. Run `VX tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts` and see all four return `false`. Then in `TX` add `import { isNoEditRequest } from '../command-attach.js';` below the module header and replace the line that starts `const explicitNoWrite = /\\b(no edits?|without making changes|` with `const explicitNoWrite = isNoEditRequest(promptLower);`. Verify: the first run fails four cases, then `VX tests/scorer/read-only-explainer.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `rg -c \"without making changes\" $TX` prints nothing.\n83: - [ ] T005 [P] Route the scorer's two command gates through the shared helper (`FU`, `CMA`). Test first: in `CMA`, inside `describe('commandMeaningEligible')`, add `it('rules out every command when the prompt asks for no change with a curly apostrophe')` with the prompt `'walk me through the optional behaviour toggles, don\\u2019t touch anything'`, expecting `commandMeaningEligible(prompt, false, mutatingCommand)` and `commandMeaningEligible(prompt, false, readOnlyCommand)` to be `false`. Run `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` and see the new case return `true`. Then in `FU` replace `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` with `isNoEditRequest` in the import from `'../command-attach.js'`, and replace both `NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(promptLower)` calls, the one in `readOnlyRouteAllowed` and the one in `commandMeaningEligible`, with `isNoEditRequest(promptLower)`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c \"isNoEditRequest\\(promptLower\\)\" $FU` prints 2, `rg -c \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $FU` prints nothing and `TC` exits 0.\n84: - [ ] T006 [P] Make the status privacy case store what it guards (`AST`). Keep the case name `does not leak prompt content in status output`. After `writeGeneration(root, 'live', 5);`, save `process.env.SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`, set it to `'1'`, await `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord(root, createAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord({ runtime: 'claude', status: 'ok', freshness: 'live', durationMs: 10, cacheHit: true, skillLabel: 'privacy-marker-skill', errorDetails: 'secret@example.com' }))` and restore the variable in a `finally`, as the case `reports hook health from durable diagnostic records` does. Then expect `readFileSync(advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(root), 'utf8')` to contain `privacy-marker-skill` and `secret@example.com`, keep the two `not.toContain` lines on `raw`, add `expect(raw).not.toContain('privacy-marker-skill')` and expect `JSON.parse(raw).data.hookHealth.invocations` to be 1. This case passes today, because status carries aggregates only, and it guards that. Verify: `VX tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node TSX $PL/probe-status-privacy.mts` prints `privacy case persists a record: true`.\n85: - [ ] T007 [P] Drop the attach assertion that never reaches a gate (`CAT`). In the case `offers a deep-loop command only when the prompt asks for that effort`, delete the line `expect(attachCommand('sk-doc', singleRoute('sk-create-benchmark'), PLAIN_PROMPT, INJECTED)).toBeUndefined();` and keep the next line, which proves the gate belongs to the deep-loop hub alone. Verify: `rg -c \"singleRoute\\('sk-create-benchmark'\\), PLAIN_PROMPT\" $CAT` prints nothing and `VX tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n86: - [ ] T008 [P] Name every command row field in the command-bridges README (`CBR`, `CAG`). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('generated command table')`, add `it('the command-bridges README names every command row field')`, which reads `join(import.meta.dirname, '../lib/command-attach.ts')` and `join(import.meta.dirname, '../scripts/command-bridges/README.md')` with `readFileSync` (import it from `node:fs` and `join` from `node:path` when absent), takes the field names from the `export interface CommandRow {` block with `/readonly (\\w+)\\??:/g`, expects them to equal `['command', 'policy', 'mutating', 'ownerSkillId']` and expects the README sentence that starts `Each row carries` to contain each name wrapped in backticks. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see it fail on the first name. Then in `CBR` replace the sentence `Each row carries the runnable slash command, its derived policy and the owning skill.` with ``Each row carries `command`, the runnable slash command, `policy`, its derived policy, `mutating`, the class that says what a run writes (`read-only`, `add-only` or `mutates`) when the record names one, and `ownerSkillId`, the owning skill.`` Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `rg -c \"its derived policy and the owning skill\" $CBR` prints nothing.\n87: - [ ] T009 [P] Escape line breaks in generated string literals (`DER`, `DCS`). Test first: create `DCS` with the module banner the other test files use and a comment saying a generated literal holding a raw line break no longer parses, so the generated source would stop compiling. Load `DER` with `createRequire(import.meta.url)` as `tests/command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` does, and add `it.each([['LF', 'a\\nb'], ['CR', 'a\\rb'], ['U+2028', 'a\\u2028b'], ['U+2029', 'a\\u2029b'], ['a quote and a backslash', \"it's a \\\\ path\"]])('round-trips a value holding %s', (_label, value) => ...)`, expecting `tsString(value)` to match `/^'[^\\n\\r\\u2028\\u2029]*'$/` and `new Function('return ' + tsString(value) + ';')()` to equal `value`. Run `VX tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` and see it fail because `tsString` is not exported. Then in `DER` add `tsString` to `module.exports`, and in `tsString` chain `.replaceAll('\\n', '\\\\n').replaceAll('\\r', '\\\\r').replaceAll('\\u2028', '\\\\u2028').replaceAll('\\u2029', '\\\\u2029')` after the two existing `replaceAll` calls. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `DERIVE` prints `{\"status\":\"fresh\",\"changed\":[]}` and `node $PL/probe-tsstring.cjs` prints `exported: true` and `parses true` on its four break lines.\n88: \n89: ### Wave 1, lane WG2: behaviour runner replay and restore\n90: - [ ] T010 [P] Run no code from an untrusted backfill checkout (`CO`, `COT`). Test first: in `COT`, inside `describe('backfillRunLog')`, add `it('runs nothing from a checkout that is neither the project root nor a marked arena')`: make a temporary folder holding a fake `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` and a fake `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`, each writing its own marker file into that folder when run, write a one-line log whose `locator.projectDir` names the folder, call `backfillRunLog` with `promptFor: () => 'prompt'`, `brief: async () => 'unknown'` and the default warm and replay, and expect `ok` true, `lines` 1, `offerError` `untrusted_checkout` on the written line and neither marker file. Add `it('replays a checkout that holds the arena marker')`, where the folder also holds `.git/skilled-behaviour-arena` and stub `warm` and `replay` record their `checkoutDir`, expecting both to record that folder. Run `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` and see the first case fail because both fakes ran. Then in `CO` add `realpathSync` to the `node:fs` import and `export function trustedCheckout(checkoutDir)`, which returns `true` when `realpathSync(checkoutDir)` equals `realpathSync(REPO_ROOT)` or `existsSync(join(checkoutDir, '.git', 'skilled-behaviour-arena'))` holds, and `false` when either call throws, with a comment that a run log is input and the folder it names may hold any code. Give `backfillRunLog` a `trusted = trustedCheckout` option, named in its jsdoc, and before the warm-up, when `checkoutDir !== null && !trusted(checkoutDir)`, set the offer to `{ offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'untrusted_checkout' }` and skip the warm-up and the replay. In the existing case `adds the offer and the brief to every line and warms each checkout o